# Copy to .env (gitignored).

# THE QUANTISATION LADDER. Sizes are the sum of every shard, which is what has
# to land on the disk. A stock node has ~515 GB free, so the line between
# "runs" and "cannot be stored" falls between IQ1_M and Q2_K:
#
#   IQ1_S     337 GB   6block          <- default. 1-bit, and the trade is real
#   IQ1_M     372 GB   6block          <- +35 GB for a less aggressive 1-bit
#   Q2_K      569 GB   DevQuasar          needs external storage from here down
#   Q2_K-XL   574 GB   teamblobfish
#   IQ3_XXS   620 GB   6block
#   Q3_K_M    652 GB   6block
#   Q4_K_M    951 GB   DevQuasar
#   Q8_0     1672 GB   teamblobfish
#
# None of them fit in MEMORY - that is not what this ladder is choosing
# between. It is choosing how much disk gets read per token, and how much
# quality you give up for it.

# The next rung up, if IQ1_S disappoints and you have the space:
# MODEL_FILE=DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-IQ1_M.gguf

# 2-bit, which needs external storage. ~570 GB against ~515 GB free:
# HF_HOME=/mnt/big/hf
# MODEL_REPO=teamblobfish/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-GGUF
# MODEL_FILE=Q2_K-XL/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-Q2_K-XL-00001-of-00013.gguf
# NEED_DISK_GB=600

# Context. 8192, which is small on purpose: every token of context is KV cache
# competing for the same page cache that is the only thing making mmap
# tolerable. Raising it makes the paging worse, not just the memory tighter.
# CTX=8192

# Sampling. DeepSeek's published values; top_p 0.95 for agentic use.
# TEMP=1.0
# TOP_P=1.0
# MIN_P=0.01

# The startup disk guard. Lowering it does not create space - it only moves
# where you find out, from "before the download" to "at 94% of it, with a full
# root filesystem". Raise it when you switch to a larger quant above.
# NEED_DISK_GB=360

# PORT=8892
